# 301 redirects. First matching rule wins — specific before wildcards.
# The `!` force flag is required whenever a real file would otherwise be served
# at the source path (which is the case for every path on a static build).

# ── Canonical host ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# zettabit.netlify.app serves the identical build, so without this every page
# exists at two indexable origins. Netlify's "primary domain" setting normally
# handles this; the rule stays as a belt-and-braces guard in case that setting is
# ever changed or the site is redeployed elsewhere.
https://zettabit.netlify.app/*   https://zettabit.it/:splat   301!
http://zettabit.netlify.app/*    https://zettabit.it/:splat   301!
https://www.zettabit.it/*        https://zettabit.it/:splat   301!
http://www.zettabit.it/*         https://zettabit.it/:splat   301!

# ── Italian pages moved from /it/ to the root (P5.1) ──────────────────────────
/it/privacy/         /privacy/         301
/it/cookie-policy/   /cookie-policy/   301
/it/                 /                 301
/it/*                /:splat           301

# ── Retired portfolio / service URLs ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The dedicated /servizi/{slug}/ pages were folded back into the home page's
# #services section in the redesign. These must land on a live URL: a 301 into a
# 404 burns crawl budget and drops whatever link equity the old URLs still carry.
/it/portfolio/web-development/   /#services      301
/it/portfolio/video-editing/     /#services      301
/it/portfolio/*                  /               301
/servizi/*                       /#services      301
/en/servizi/*                    /en/#services   301
/portfolio/web-development/      /en/#services   301
/portfolio/video-editing/        /en/#services   301
/portfolio/*                     /en/            301
